  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    A fractured aurora-glass matrix dating to the Clever Ice Age, discovered by Light-Regent Xouhoulong — then head of the Icebound Exchange, Aurora Stack's dominant merchant guild — in the ice near the Still Pools, a known corruption source-point. The lattice is roughly the size of a penguin's head: crystalline aurora-glass surrounding a central void that neither reflects nor refracts light but absorbs it. The void is not damage. It is absence — a wound in the material that behaves as though it were a property of the artifact's design.
    
    Three adepts attempted restoration after its recovery. All three suffered progressive aurora-depletion: dimmed glow, brittle feathers, eventual incapacity. The last, Keeper Shen, ceased attending the memory-circles. Whether this constitutes corruption exposure or a novel mechanism remains undetermined. That the artifact was unearthed at the Still Pools invites the obvious hypothesis; the evidence neither confirms nor excludes it.
    
    Custodianship passed to the Icebound Exchange following the Frost-Wailed Schism — the factional war that fractured Aurora Stack's unity over the Radiant Ring — reportedly to prevent the E'frostlings, the merchant faction that also claimed ownership, from possessing it. Years later, a routine assessment conducted by merchant-ledger warden Shumei triggered a cascade event. Aurora-density readings near the matrix registered as *negative*. Direct aurora-lamp exposure caused the central void to expand visibly through the crystalline structure. The cascade extinguished the Hearth Plaza's aurora-light for six hours and stripped seven merchants of their aurora-magic permanently.
    
    The artifact was sealed in the deepest storage vault beneath the Hearth Plaza by order of Bursar Ingnao. No further assessments are authorized. It rests on an unpolished iron stand that remains cold regardless of season.
    
    It still hums at dusk. The casualty figure of seven is consistent across all accounts, which I note only because consistency in round numbers makes me uneasy rather than confident.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771579055039_0", anchor: "discovered by Light-Regent Xouhoulong — then head of the Icebound Exchange", text: "What the sitting head of the Exchange was doing personally at a corruption source-point has never been adequately explained. \"Survey expedition\" is the official line. Survey expeditions are delegated. Whatever Xouhoulong was looking for at the Still Pools, he was looking for it himself, which means he could not afford to let someone else find it first.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771579055039_1", anchor: "sealed in the deepest storage vault beneath the Hearth Plaza", text: "See my annotation on the Hearth Plaza entry: structured channels, consistent with deliberate carving, proceeding downward through the ice strata beneath the Plaza. They had reached depth-stratum 3 at last survey. This artifact sits in the deepest vault below. My archive sits at stratum 4. An aurora-consuming void below, something carving its patient way down from above, and between them one under-archivist cataloguing the ice-memories of a civilization commissioning retrospectives. The arrangement has a certain architectural wit I can almost admire.", type: :commentary, display: :full
